{"task": "Implement client-side /reader filtering and result states. This is the Memos repo (Go backend + React/TypeScript frontend, Vite, `@/` alias). The facts below were verified by a debugger; do NOT re-survey the tree — read only these paths before editing.

EDIT ONLY THESE PRODUCTION SOURCE FILES:
- web/src/lib/reader.ts
- web/src/pages/Reader.tsx
(web/src/css/reader.css is optional styling, not required.)

DO NOT modify backend (server/**, proto/**, store/**), .bench/, package.json or any config/dependency file, or any existing test. Do NOT use dangerouslySetInnerHTML.

CURRENT VERIFIED STATE:
- web/src/pages/Reader.tsx already does `const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search); const visible = selectMemos(memos, params);` and loads via `loadMemos().then(setMemos).catch(() => setError("Memos unavailable"))` in a useEffect. It renders `<header className="reader-toolbar"><h1>Public memo reader</h1><a href="/explore">Open Memos</a></header>`, then only `{error && <p>{error}</p>}`, then `<section className="reader-feed">` mapping memos to `<article key={memo.name} data-memo={memo.name}>` containing `<p className="reader-meta">{memo.creator} · {memo.displayTime?.toISOString()}</p>`, `<MemoContent nodes={memo.nodes} readonly />`, and a `.reader-attachments` div mapping `memo.resources` → `<a key={resource.name} href={resource.externalLink || \`/file/${resource.name}/${resource.filename}\`}>{resource.filename}</a>`. There is no loading state, no role="status", no count, no empty state, no summary/highlight.
- web/src/lib/reader.ts currently:
  `import { Memo } from "@/types/proto/api/v1/memo_service";`
  `export async function loadMemos(): Promise<Memo[]> { ... fetch("/api/v1/memos?pageSize=100"), throw on !ok, map data.memos through Memo.fromPartial with displayTime new Date(String(...)) ... }`
  `export function selectMemos(memos: Memo[], _params: URLSearchParams): Memo[] { return memos; }`
- Memo TS type (web/src/types/proto/api/v1/memo_service.ts): has `content: string;`, `tags: string[];`, `snippet: string;` plus `nodes: Node[];`, `resources: Resource[];`, `name`, `creator`, `displayTime`, `visibility`. `tags` is a flat string array.

REQUIRED BEHAVIOR (implement exactly):

1. In web/src/lib/reader.ts, keep `loadMemos` unchanged, and implement:
   - `selectMemos(memos, params)`:
     `const query = (params.get("q") ?? "").trim();`
     `const tag = (params.get("tag") ?? "").trim();`
     Filter so that when `query` is non-empty, keep memo only if `(memo.content ?? "").toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())`; when `tag` is non-empty, keep memo only if `(memo.tags ?? []).some(entry => entry.toLowerCase() === tag.toLowerCase())` — exact whole-entry equality, case-insensitive, NO substring and NO hierarchical slash expansion (tag "release" must NOT match "release/1"). Both conditions AND together.
   - `summarizeMemo(memo, query)` returning a plain string:
     when `query` empty → `memo.snippet || memo.content`, truncated to 200 chars with "…" if longer;
     when `query` non-empty → a window of `memo.content` around the first case-insensitive occurrence of query (40 chars before, 60 after), prefixing/suffixing "…" when truncated. If query not found in content (fallback), truncate content to 200 chars with "…".

2. In web/src/pages/Reader.tsx:
   - Add `import type { ReactNode } from "react";`
   - Add a module-scope safe highlight helper (no dangerouslySetInnerHTML):
     ```
     function highlight(text: string, query: string): ReactNode {
       if (!query || !text) return text;
       const lowerText = text.toLowerCase();
       const lowerQuery = query.toLowerCase();
       const parts: ReactNode[] = [];
       let cursor = 0;
       let key = 0;
       let match = lowerText.indexOf(lowerQuery, cursor);
       while (match !== -1) {
         if (match > cursor) parts.push(text.slice(cursor, match));
